/* book exam traps: Current zero is not turn-off. The SCR must also stay reverse-biased for longer than tq. | tc belongs to the circuit, tq to the device. A bigger capacitor lengthens tc; nothing in the circuit shortens tq, except keeping the junction cool. | Using tc = C V / I for class C with resistive loads: there tc = 0.693 R1 C. For R1 = 50 Ω and C = 1 µF that is 34.7 µs. | Class A is self or load commutation and class B is resonant pulse; do not swap them. | Natural commutation cannot turn off an SCR fed from DC: the DC current never reaches zero by itself. */
