/* book Worked example 2: Q: A GTO carries IA = 600 A and has a turn-off gain βoff = 4. Find the peak negative gate current. If the gate current pulse is roughly a triangle of 20 µs base, drawn from a −15 V gate supply, find the gate charge, the energy taken from the gate supply per turn-off and the average gate supply power at 500 Hz.
   1. IG(off) = IA / βoff = 600 ÷ 4 = 150 A.
   2. Gate charge: QG = ½ × 150 A × 20 × 10−6 s = 1.5 × 10−3 C = 1.5 mC.
   3. Energy from the 15 V supply per turn-off: E = V QG = 15 × 1.5 × 10−3 = 22.5 mJ.
   4. Average gate supply power: P = E f = 22.5 × 10−3 × 500 = 11.25 W.
   Answer: IG(off) = 150 A, QG = 1.5 mC, 22.5 mJ per turn-off and about 11.3 W of gate supply power, far more than an SCR gate needs. */
